---
id: rain_relay
title: The Rain Relay
---
=== roof
~ vane_free = false
~ shutter_open = false
A glass receiver holds yesterday's rain as a silver thread. The roof vane is caught on a ribbon; the listening shutter is closed. Jun and Tavi can each take a small part of the work. Neither needs to hold the whole mechanism in mind.
* [Free the roof vane] { vane_free == false }
  ~ vane_free = true
  -> roof
* [Open the listening shutter] { shutter_open == false }
  ~ shutter_open = true
  -> roof
* [Release the rain note] { vane_free && shutter_open }
  ~ announce "The rain draws one silver line across the listening room."
  -> listening_room
=== listening_room
The receiver is quiet. A silver line trembles above the table, waiting for a name. Leave that name on the shared rain card; the two objects keep separate histories.
* [Listen once more]
  -> listening_room
* [Carry the sound away]
  -> END
